# In-app bug reports (docs/manual-setup-bug-reporting.md, part 3).
#
# Without all four Firebase values, the build has no in-app form and "Report a bug" opens GitHub's
# form instead. They are public identifiers, not secrets (Firebase web config and a reCAPTCHA site
# key are visible to every visitor anyway), so the production values go in `.env.production`,
# committed, where CI's build picks them up.

# Firebase console → Project settings → General → Your apps → the web app's config.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=meridian-web-a5829
# Google Cloud console → Security → reCAPTCHA (Fraud Defense) → the score-based web key's ID.
VITE_RECAPTCHA_ENTERPRISE_SITE_KEY=

# Development only (`npm run dev`), ignored in production builds. Put these in
# `.env.development.local` (gitignored by `*.local`):
# Send reports to the Functions emulator without App Check (the emulator doesn't check).
# VITE_BUG_REPORT_EMULATOR=true
# Or use App Check's debug provider against the real App Check service (register the token the
# console prints: Firebase console → App Check → Apps → ⋮ → Manage debug tokens).
# VITE_APPCHECK_DEBUG=true
